---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Icons" description="How to use a third-party icon set with Farn — sizing and colour driven by Farn tokens">
  <h1>Icons</h1>
  <span class="badge badge-beta">guide</span>
  <p>
    Farn does not ship an icon set. Icons are a large, opinionated surface — hundreds of glyphs,
    multiple weights, a release cadence of their own — and bundling one would tie Farn to choices
    that belong to your project, not the token layer. Instead, Farn gives you the <em>sizing</em>
    and <em>colour</em> tokens to make any third-party set feel native.
  </p>

  <h2>Recommended library</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://lucide.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Lucide</strong></a>
    is the recommended default — 1,700+ icons, ISC licence, a clean stroke character that sits
    naturally with Farn's restrained aesthetic, and every icon uses <code>currentColor</code> out
    of the box. It is the only library in the space with an official <code>lucide-astro</code>
    package, and the <code>lucide-static</code> package ships individual SVG files for any
    framework or no framework at all.
  </p>

  <h3>Install</h3>
  <pre><code># Astro — official component package
npm install lucide-astro

# Vanilla / any bundler — individual SVG files
npm install lucide-static</code></pre>

  <h3>Inline SVG (vanilla)</h3>
  <p>
    Browse <a href="https://lucide.dev/icons" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">lucide.dev/icons</a>,
    click an icon, and copy the <code>&lt;svg&gt;</code> markup. Paste it directly into your HTML.
    The default <code>stroke="currentColor"</code> means the icon inherits the surrounding text
    colour without any extra CSS.
  </p>
  <pre><code>&lt;!-- Paste any icon from lucide.dev — stroke="currentColor" is the default --&gt;
&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
     width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
     fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
     stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
     aria-hidden="true"&gt;
  &lt;path d="M5 12h14"/&gt;
  &lt;path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;</code></pre>

  <h3>Astro components</h3>
  <pre><code>---
import &#123; ArrowRight, Check, Info &#125; from 'lucide-astro';
---

&lt;!-- Decorative icon next to a label --&gt;
&lt;button&gt;
  &lt;ArrowRight size=&#123;20&#125; aria-hidden="true" /&gt;
  Continue
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;!-- Icon-only control — label goes on the button, not the icon --&gt;
&lt;button aria-label="Next page"&gt;
  &lt;ArrowRight size=&#123;20&#125; aria-hidden="true" /&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>

  <div class="demo-surface icon-aside">
    <strong>Need more?</strong>
    <a href="https://phosphoricons.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Phosphor</a>
    offers six weights including duotone — the only free library with native two-tone icons.
    <a href="https://tabler.io/icons" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tabler</a>
    (6,100+ icons) suits dashboards and data-heavy products.
    Both use <code>currentColor</code> and work with the same sizing and colour patterns below.
  </div>

  <h2>Size with spacing tokens</h2>
  <p>
    Drive icon dimensions from the spacing scale so they track the rest of the system. As a rule of
    thumb: inline icons match the surrounding cap height; standalone affordances sit one step up.
  </p>

  <div class="demo-surface icon-size-demo">
    <div class="size-row">
      <span class="size-label">Inline with text</span>
      <span class="size-preview">
        Read the
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1em" height="1em" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align:-0.125em"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        docs
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="size-row">
      <span class="size-label">Button / input (<code>--space-md</code>, 24px)</span>
      <span class="size-preview">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:var(--space-md);height:var(--space-md)" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="size-row">
      <span class="size-label">Standalone / feature (<code>--space-lg</code>, 36px)</span>
      <span class="size-preview">
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:var(--space-lg);height:var(--space-lg)" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Context</th><th>Token</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Inline with text</td><td><code>1em</code></td><td>tracks font-size</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Button / input affordance</td><td><code>--space-md</code></td><td>24px</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Standalone / feature</td><td><code>--space-lg</code></td><td>36px</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <pre><code>.icon &#123;
  width: var(--space-md);   /* 24px — button and input icons */
  height: var(--space-md);
&#125;

.icon-inline &#123;
  width: 1em;               /* tracks surrounding text size */
  height: 1em;
  vertical-align: -0.125em; /* optical baseline nudge */
&#125;

.icon-feature &#123;
  width: var(--space-lg);   /* 36px — standalone callout or feature icon */
  height: var(--space-lg);
&#125;</code></pre>

  <h2>Colour with semantic tokens</h2>
  <p>
    Control icon colour through the parent's <code>color</code> property — SVG icons inherit it
    via <code>currentColor</code> regardless of whether they use stroke or fill. Lucide uses
    <code>stroke="currentColor"</code> by default; Phosphor Fill and Tabler filled variants use
    <code>fill="currentColor"</code>. Either way, Farn's semantic tokens resolve per theme and
    surface, so an icon coloured with <code>var(--color-text)</code> stays legible everywhere —
    no dark-mode overrides needed.
  </p>

  <div class="demo-surface icon-colour-demo">
    <div class="colour-swatch colour-text">
      <svg class="swatch-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/>
        <circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/>
      </svg>
      <code>--color-text</code>
    </div>
    <div class="colour-swatch colour-accent">
      <svg class="swatch-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"/>
      </svg>
      <code>--color-accent</code>
    </div>
    <div class="colour-swatch colour-secondary">
      <svg class="swatch-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
        <path d="M12 16v-4"/>
        <path d="M12 8h.01"/>
      </svg>
      <code>--color-text-secondary</code>
    </div>
    <div class="colour-swatch colour-error">
      <svg class="swatch-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z"/>
        <path d="M12 9v4"/>
        <path d="M12 17h.01"/>
      </svg>
      <code>--color-error</code>
    </div>
    <div class="colour-swatch colour-success">
      <svg class="swatch-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/>
      </svg>
      <code>--color-success</code>
    </div>
  </div>

  <pre><code>/* Drive icon colour through the parent — icons inherit currentColor */
.icon-accent   &#123; color: var(--color-accent); &#125;
.icon-muted    &#123; color: var(--color-text-secondary); &#125;
.icon-error    &#123; color: var(--color-error); &#125;
.icon-success  &#123; color: var(--color-success); &#125;</code></pre>

  <p>
    Toggle the page theme to verify — the demo icons above adapt to light, dark, and every
    <code>data-surface</code> context automatically.
  </p>

  <h2>Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Decorative icon (next to a label)</strong> — add <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>.
      The visible text already conveys the meaning; the icon is presentational.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Icon-only control (no visible label)</strong> — put the accessible name on the
      interactive element (<code>aria-label</code> on the <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>),
      and add <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> to the icon itself.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Standalone icon conveying meaning</strong> — use <code>role="img"</code> and
      a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> inside the SVG so screen readers announce it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Colour alone</strong> — never use icon colour as the sole state signal. Pair a
      semantic colour with a distinct shape or a visible label.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <pre><code>&lt;!-- Decorative — icon sits next to a text label --&gt;
&lt;button&gt;
  &lt;svg aria-hidden="true"&gt;...&lt;/svg&gt;
  Save changes
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;!-- Icon-only control — accessible name lives on the button --&gt;
&lt;button aria-label="Close dialog"&gt;
  &lt;svg aria-hidden="true"&gt;...&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;!-- Standalone meaningful icon — title is read aloud --&gt;
&lt;svg role="img" aria-labelledby="icon-title"&gt;
  &lt;title id="icon-title"&gt;Warning&lt;/title&gt;
  ...
&lt;/svg&gt;</code></pre>
</DocLayout>

<style>
  .icon-aside {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: var(--space-lg) 0;
  }

  .icon-size-demo {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  .size-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .size-label {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    min-width: 280px;
  }

  .size-preview {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .icon-colour-demo {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  .colour-swatch {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .colour-swatch code {
    font-size: 0.75em;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .swatch-icon {
    width: var(--space-lg);
    height: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .colour-text     { color: var(--color-text); }
  .colour-accent   { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .colour-secondary { color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .colour-error    { color: var(--color-error); }
  .colour-success  { color: var(--color-success); }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .size-label { min-width: 0; }
    .size-row   { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
  }
</style>
